@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/json-patch.ts` already has private helpers (`isObject`, `setMember`, `clone`) that avoid prototype pollution and aliasing.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New file `src/json-merge-patch.ts`; the helpers are not exported from json-patch.ts, so a small copy of them lives there rather than refactoring existing code.
+- Recursive algorithm straight from RFC 7386 section 2, building a new object; target members are cloned, patch values are cloned with null members stripped (equivalent to merging into `{}`).
+- Members are set with `Object.defineProperty` so `__proto__` is an own property.
+- Never throws: every JSON value is a valid patch.
